# See GOVERNANCE.md for how these roles are defined and how membership in
# each team is granted. The split below is deliberate: the core team owns
# the contract (spec/, schema/, vectors/) but is not a bottleneck on
# ordinary provider work (providers/), which adapter reviewers can approve
# on their own. Anything touching a closed enum, the expression language,
# or the manifest schema still requires the RFC process in GOVERNANCE.md
# regardless of who technically has approval rights to merge it.

/spec/                      @esiipayment/maintainers
/schema/                    @esiipayment/maintainers
/vectors/                   @esiipayment/maintainers
/tools/                     @esiipayment/maintainers
/.github/                   @esiipayment/maintainers
/providers/                 @esiipayment/adapter-reviewers
/providers/_template/       @esiipayment/maintainers
/providers/mock/            @esiipayment/maintainers
/docs/                      @esiipayment/maintainers
/GOVERNANCE.md              @esiipayment/maintainers
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @esiipayment/maintainers
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md         @esiipayment/maintainers
/SECURITY.md                @esiipayment/maintainers
